 "scenery": [],
 "par": {
  "time": 600
 },
 "intro": {
  "title": "HARMONIC GARDENS",
  "lines": [
   "A garden sunk in a bowl of terraces, and a tree at the bottom of it.",
   "Every plant in it was grown to ring."
  ]
 },
 "outro": "The third wall opens on a stair. Behind you the garden is still ringing, very faintly, in a chord you did not play.",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "start",
   "at": [41, 64],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "A garden in a bowl. Stone beds on a spiral down every terrace, each a little further round than the last. Whoever laid it out did not use a line or a plumb. They used a count."
  },
  {
   "id": "harvest",
   "at": [41, 57],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Spearmen in green walking the beds with long hooks, picking."
  },
  {
   "id": "plate",
   "at": [41, 49],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "RINGING PLATE",
   "text": "Run a nail down it: five plants, five notes. A gardener grows one for each, and lays the bed so that a tone from one strikes the next."
  },
  {
   "id": "tree",
   "at": [41, 46],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The tree in the middle plays a phrase when you use it: the fruit light in order, a note each. Answer on the chimes, in order, each within eight seconds of the last."
  },
  {
   "id": "avenue",
   "at": [41, 22],
   "radius": 4,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "Three walls across the avenue out of the bowl. The tree plays the next phrase that is not yet answered. A wrong note starts the phrase again."
  },
  {
   "id": "r1",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Three notes, and the first wall has gone back into its bed. It folded. Like a hedge in a wind."
  },
  {
   "id": "r2",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Four. The second wall. The tree is a count: three, four, and I suppose five."
  },
  {
   "id": "r3",
   "at": [1, 1],
   "radius": 0.1,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "Five, and the last wall is open. It was a count the whole way, and the first time the Song has been one I could repeat."
  },
  {
   "id": "hollow",
   "at": [65, 43],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "HULL",
   "text": "The east rim of the garden rings hollow behind a bed with no plant in it."
  },
  {
   "id": "grove",
   "at": [69, 43],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "A SILENT (NOTE)",
   "text": "The seed of the chimes is pressed for oil. This is the last pressing before the count was called. Whoever has a lantern, take it."
  },
  {
   "id": "split",
   "at": [12, 40],
   "radius": 2,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The gardener's lodge. Hooks, twine, a bench, and the back wall split from the floor up where the roots have got into it. A shot would open it."
  },
  {
   "id": "lodge",
   "at": [8, 40],
   "radius": 1.5,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The gardener kept a rifle's worth of carbine rounds behind the wall, the tips packed in slag. For pests, I imagine."
  },
  {
   "id": "end",
   "at": [41, 6],
   "radius": 3,
   "speaker": "INES",
   "text": "The stair is cut very wide, and the steps are worn on both sides and not in the middle, as though the ones who used it were carrying something between them."
  }
 ],
 "objective": "Go down into the garden. The tree at the bottom plays a phrase: answer it on the chimes. Three phrases open the three walls",
